tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:6939b9dad78d364d7d6d519599cbc77519cd4ae9732149bf0bd13bb28d04219b","file":"preprints/Polynomial-Time-Unitary-Synthesis-from-a-Boolean-Oracle-October-5-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":46,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"51f21ce621a1a1ae271caf24402f8e57fd7a3fc1a9b4747bda4ae763574cbe35","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Polynomial-Time-Unitary-Synthesis-from-a-Boolean-Oracle-October-5-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:6939b9dad78d364d7d6d519599cbc77519cd4ae9732149bf0bd13bb28d04219b","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Polynomial-Time-Unitary-Synthesis-from-a-Boolean-Oracle-October-5-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L46"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere are a polynomial $p$ and a deterministic classical algorithm which, on\ninput $1^n$ for any integer $n\\ge1$, outputs in time at most $p(n)$ a quantum\noracle circuit $A_n$ with the following properties.  The circuit uses the gates\n$H,T,T^\\dagger,\\mathrm{CNOT}$ and a single Boolean oracle of input length\n$m(n)\\le p(n)$.  Its total number of qubits, elementary gates, and oracle calls\nare each at most $p(n)$.  For every unitary $U\\in U(2^n)$ there is a function\n$f:\\{0,1\\}^{m(n)}\\to\\{0,1\\}$ for which the output channel $\\Phi_{n,f}$ of\n$A_n^{O_f}$ satisfies\n\\[\n \\norm{\\Phi_{n,f}-\\mathcal U}_\\diamond\\le\\frac12.\n\\]"}
